  "id": "SL-057",
  "title": "Clock divider and prescaler (including odd 50 % duty)",
  "level": "E",
  "tools": "Verilog RTL, Icarus Verilog, VCD frequency/duty measurement",
  "summary": "Divide a 100 MHz clock by 2, 3, 5, 10 and 1000 with exact 50 % duty \u2014 including odd ratios that need both clock edges \u2014 and measure frequency and duty from the waveform.",
  "problem": "Dividing by an even number is easy. How do you divide by 3 or 5 and still get a 50 % duty cycle, and what does it cost?",
  "theory": "Even N: toggle every N/2 input cycles \u2192 $f/N$, 50 % duty. Odd N with a single edge gives duty\n$\\lfloor N/2\\rfloor/N$ (33 % for N = 3). ORing a rising-edge and a falling-edge version of the same\ncounter output (shifted by half an input period) gives $\\frac{(N-1)/2 + 1/2}{N}=50\\,\\%$ exactly.",
  "method": "Parameterised divider module with an odd/even generate branch. Input clock 100 MHz (10 ns). Python measures\neach output's period and high time from the VCD.",
  "track": "Signal Lab \u2014 214 electrical-engineering projects",
  "category": "C. Digital logic & HDL",
